<title>UK: Chevy Chase MCCT sets $271.5 mln asset-backed bond.</title>
<headline>Chevy Chase MCCT sets $271.5 mln asset-backed bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chevy Chase Master Credit Card Trust 2, 1996-C has issued a two-tranche bond for a total of $271.5 million, lead manager J.P. Morgan said.</p>
<p>Legal final maturity is May 2007 with the expected maturity December 15, 2003.</p>
<p>Class A notes total $246 million, and are rated triple-A by Moody's and Standard &amp; Poor's. Pricing is due later over one-month Libor.</p>
<p>Class B notes total $25.5 million and are rated single-A.</p>
<p>The issue is listed in Luxembourg and will be sold in denominations of $1,000. It is governed by New York law.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7748</p>
